   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch7/q1",
   "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}-\\dfrac12&amp;-\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\\\[4pt]\\dfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}&amp;-\\dfrac12\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Describe fully the single geometrical transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\"></span> represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span>, represented by the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\times2\"></span> matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf B\"></span>, is a reflection in the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-x\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li>Write down the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf B\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\"></span> followed by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> is the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>, which is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf C\"></span>,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"3\"><li>find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf C\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Show that there is a real number <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> for which the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,k)\"></span> is invariant under <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol>",
