   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch7/q2",
   "question": "<ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A=\\begin{pmatrix}2&amp;a\\\\a-4&amp;b\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are non-zero constants.<br>Given that the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\"></span> is self-inverse,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> and the possible values for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol><p>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf A\"></span> represents a linear transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\"></span>.<br>Using the smaller value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> from part (a),</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li>show that the invariant points of the linear transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"M\"></span> form a line, stating the equation of this line. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol></li><li><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf P=\\begin{pmatrix}p&amp;2p\\\\-1&amp;3p\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span> is a positive constant.<br>The matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf P\"></span> represents a linear transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\"></span>.<br>The triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> has vertices at the points with coordinates (1, 2), (3, 2) and (2, 5).<br>The area of the image of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> under the linear transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\"></span> is 15</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Determine the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></li></ol><p>The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> consists of a stretch scale factor 3 parallel to the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis invariant followed by a stretch scale factor <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-2\"></span> parallel to the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis with the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis invariant. The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf Q\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li>Write down the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf Q\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"U\"></span> followed by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> is the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"W\"></span>, which is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf R\"></span>,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"3\"><li>find the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf R\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol></li></ol>",
