   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch7/q4",
   "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M=\\begin{pmatrix}4&amp;-5\\\\2&amp;-7\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Show that the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span> is non-singular. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span> of the plane is represented by the matrix <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf M\"></span>.</p><p>The triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is transformed to the triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S\"></span> by the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>.</p><p>Given that the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S\"></span> is 63 square units,</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li>find the area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Show that the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2x\"></span> is invariant under the transformation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"T\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
