   "id": "pmt/pure-core-1/ch7/q6",
   "question": "<blockquote><p><em>With respect to the <strong>right-hand rule</strong>, a rotation through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta^\\circ\"></span> anticlockwise about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis is represented by the matrix</em></p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}\\cos\\theta&amp;0&amp;\\sin\\theta\\\\0&amp;1&amp;0\\\\-\\sin\\theta&amp;0&amp;\\cos\\theta\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></div></blockquote><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> has coordinates (8, 3, 2)</p><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> is the image of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> under the transformation reflection in the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=0\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\"><li>Write down the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> is the image of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> under the transformation rotation through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"120^\\circ\"></span> anticlockwise about the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis, with respect to the <strong>right-hand rule</strong>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"a\" start=\"2\"><li>Determine the exact coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Hence find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|\\overrightarrow{PR}|\"></span> giving your answer as a simplified surd. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\overrightarrow{PR}\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\overrightarrow{PQ}\"></span> are perpendicular. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li><li>Hence determine the exact area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"PQR\"></span>, giving your answer as a surd in simplest form. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
